          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#ResolutionBySpheresTouchingAlongADynkinDiagram Resolution by spheres touching along a Dynkin diagram
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/blow-up"} blow-up
            of an ADE-singularity is given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+spheres"} Riemann spheres
            that touch each other such as to form the shape of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dynkin+diagram"} Dynkin diagram
            whose A-D-E label corresponds to that of the given
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroup+of+SU%282%29"} finite subgroup of SU(2)
          %p
            This statement is originally due to (
            %a{:href => "#duVal1934I"}> duVal 1934 I, p. 1-3 (453-455)
            ). A description in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyper-K%C3%A4hler+geometry"} hyper-Kähler geometry
            is due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Kronheimer89a"} Kronheimer 89a
          %p
            Quick survey of this fact is in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Reid87"} Reid 87
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Slodowy80"} Slodowy 80
          %p#InStringTheory
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            this fact is interpreted in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+enhancement"} gauge enhancement
            of the
            = succeed "-lift" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MK6"} MK6
            at an ADE-singularity (
            %a{:href => "enhanced+gauge+symmetry#Sen97"}> Sen 97
            ):
          %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/ADESingularity.jpg", :width => "760px"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#HSS18"} HSS18
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+lift+of+gauge+enhancement+on+D6-branes"} M-theory lift of gauge enhancement on D6-branes
            for more.
