          %h3#bridgeland_stability_conditions Bridgeland stability conditions
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi ADE
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_{ADE} \subset SU(2)
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroup+of+SU%282%29"} finite subgroup of SU(2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde X
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution+of+singularities"} resolution
            of the corresponding ADE-singularity as
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ResolutionBySpheresTouchingAlongADynkinDiagram"} above
          %p
            Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
            of the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bridgeland+stability+conditions"} Bridgeland stability conditions
            on the bounded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde X
            can be described explicitly (
            %a{:href => "#Bridgeland05"}> Bridgeland 05
            ).
          %p
            Specifically for type-A singularities the space of stability conditions is in fact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply-connected+topological+space"} simply-connected topological space
            (
            %a{:href => "#IshiiUedaUehara10"}> Ishii-Ueda-Uehara 10
            ).
          %p
            Brief review is in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Bridgeland09"} Bridgeland 09, section 6.3
